# Copyrighted course textbook, and everything extracted from it.
#
# The book is Stallings, Computer Organization and Architecture, 10th ed. The
# EXTRACTED TEXT IS THE SAME COPYRIGHTED WORK -- slicing a PDF does not create a
# new one -- so both stay out of the repository. What IS committed is the
# authored lesson content under content/stages/, which is original prose written
# from the book and citing it, plus short quoted definitions.
#
# Anyone rebuilding this needs their own copy of the book and one command:
#   pnpm book:extract
*.pdf
!docs/source/CPE 412.docx.pdf
docs/source/book/

# Playwright MCP captures. Screenshots of the deployed apps, taken during design
# review -- evidence for a conversation, not source. They also contain whatever
# was on screen at the time, which on the console means real student names, so
# they must never be committed.
.playwright/

# design/ -- the redesign's visual pass (docs/redesign/FOLDER-STRUCTURE.md).
# Split deliberately: a small permanent contract is committed, the large
# disposable output is not.
#
#   design/templates/    COMMITTED. One reference screenshot per route.
#   design/baselines/    COMMITTED. Playwright's snapshotDir. Machine-managed.
#   design/specs/        COMMITTED. The capture specs themselves.
#   design/screenshots/  ignored -- ad-hoc dev captures, dated subfolders.
#   design/qa-report/    ignored -- Playwright's HTML reporter output.
#
# Same reasoning as .playwright/ above, and it binds harder on the two
# committed folders because they are permanent: fixture data only, never a
# real student or teacher name.
design/screenshots/
design/qa-report/
